Local Optimize on Debian/Ubuntu
================================

The Ubuntu 26.04/amd64 package installs application code, dependency lock
metadata and model policy under /usr/lib/local-optimize. During package
configuration (postinst), "local-optimize sync" provisions a shared
Python 3.14 Intel XPU environment in /var/lib/local-optimize/venv, downloads
or updates the HuggingFace E5/Qwen models in /var/lib/local-optimize/models,
and verifies/pulls qwen2.5-coder:7b in the local Ollama service.
Use an SSD for /var/lib/local-optimize and /usr/share/ollama.

Prerequisites are an Intel GPU driver/OpenCL ICD, PostgreSQL 18 with pgvector,
and an installed, running Ollama binary/service with the ollama system user.
PostgreSQL, pgvector and python3-venv are package dependencies. Ollama is
checked by preinst because this host installs it outside dpkg.

Configure ~/.config/local-optimize/secrets.env and projects.json as described
in /usr/share/doc/local-optimize/docs/installation.md. Package installation
cannot safely invent database credentials or bearer tokens. Keep real secrets
out of the repository.

Commands:

  sudo local-optimize sync      Provision/update venv and models
  local-optimize models status  Check local vs upstream/policy model state
  local-optimize migrate        Apply PostgreSQL migrations
  local-optimize server         Run the FastAPI server
  local-optimize watchdog       Run filesystem indexing
  local-optimize mcp            Run the full local-only MCP server
  local-optimize lmstudio-mcp   Run the read-only LM Studio MCP wrapper
  local-optimize index          Index the registered project

LOCAL_OPTIMIZE_VENV can override /var/lib/local-optimize/venv for development.
LOCAL_OPTIMIZE_MODELS_DIR can override /var/lib/local-optimize/models.
LOCAL_OPTIMIZE_ROOT can override /usr/lib/local-optimize for packaging checks.

The user units are installed but not globally enabled. After configuration,
apply migrations and check the server, then enable them for the intended user:

  local-optimize migrate
  systemctl --user enable --now gpu-rag-server.service watchdog-indexer.service

On startup, gpu-rag-server.service also runs "local-optimize migrate" via
ExecStartPre, and apt upgrades automatically reload systemd --user and
try-restart already active user services.

Verify /liveness, /readiness and /runtime before registering local-only agents.
Cloud-capable clients must not receive direct RAG MCP access. Existing allowed
agent entries should use /usr/bin/local-optimize mcp (or lmstudio-mcp for the
isolated LM Studio wrapper).
